---
import { getEntry } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import VideoEmbed from '../components/VideoEmbed.astro';

// Reuse the real clip registry so the demo below is the actual product,
// not a mock-up.
const demo = await getEntry('embeds', 'olah-vatican-2026');
const d = demo?.data;

const embedSnippet = `<iframe
  src="https://civicinterplay.io/embed/olah-vatican-2026"
  style="width:100%; border:0; aspect-ratio:16/9"
  loading="lazy"
  allowfullscreen
  title="Civic Interplay video player"
></iframe>`;

// DRAFT copy. Sarah to revise wording.
---
<BaseLayout
  title="A video player that doesn't watch you back"
  description="A small video player built as a counter-model: no third-party scripts, no cookies, self-hosted media, captioned and portable by default."
>
  <article>
    <div class="narrow">
      <div class="post-header">
        <div class="post-tag" style="color: var(--purple)">The player</div>
        <h1>A video player that doesn't watch you back</h1>
      </div>

      <div class="post-content">
        <p class="lede"><em>This is a draft. A small video player, built as a counter-model.</em></p>

        <p>
          Most embedded players are surveillance instruments wearing a play button. They
          set cookies, load third-party scripts, log who watched what and for how long, and
          feed it back into a recommendation machine you don't control. Until recently this
          one quietly did some of that too: it pulled its typeface from Google's servers, so
          every viewer's browser phoned home before the video even started. We noticed. We
          fixed it.
        </p>

        <p>
          Now it doesn't. The media sits on our own storage. There are no third-party
          scripts, no cookies, no tracking pixels, no algorithm deciding what you see next.
          If Civic Interplay disappeared tomorrow, the file would still play and you could
          still download it.
        </p>

        <p>
          It is a tiny thing. But sovereignty over infrastructure starts with small
          refusals: the choice to host your own file, to not phone home, to let a viewer
          just watch.
        </p>

        {d && (
          <VideoEmbed
            src={d.video ?? ''}
            webm={d.videoWebm}
            poster={d.poster}
            caption={d.caption}
            aspectRatio={d.aspectRatio ?? '16/9'}
            title={d.title}
          />
        )}

        <h2>The promises</h2>
        <ul class="promises">
          <li><strong>No third-party scripts, no cookies.</strong> The player calls no domain but our own. Nothing to consent to.</li>
          <li><strong>Self-hosted media.</strong> The video files live on our storage, not a platform's.</li>
          <li><strong>Captioned and legible by default.</strong> Accessibility is the baseline, not an add-on.</li>
          <li><strong>Portable.</strong> Native, downloadable, and it keeps working if we don't.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Put it on your own site</h2>
        <p>Paste this wherever you can drop HTML. It loads nothing from us until someone presses play.</p>
        <pre class="embed-code"><code>{embedSnippet}</code></pre>
      </div>

      <div class="back-link">
        <a href="/">Civic Interplay</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <style>
    .lede {
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      color: var(--text-dim);
    }

    .promises {
      list-style: none;
      padding: 0;
      margin: 1.5rem 0;
    }
    .promises li {
      padding: 0.85rem 0 0.85rem 1.5rem;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border-light);
      position: relative;
      font-size: 0.98rem;
    }
    .promises li::before {
      content: '';
      position: absolute;
      left: 0;
      top: 1.15rem;
      width: 8px;
      height: 8px;
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: var(--purple);
    }
    .promises li strong {
      color: var(--text);
    }

    .embed-code {
      background: #1c1917;
      color: #f8f8f8;
      border: 2px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius);
      box-shadow: 4px 4px 0 var(--border);
      padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem;
      overflow-x: auto;
      font-size: 0.82rem;
      line-height: 1.55;
      font-family: ui-monospace, 'SFMono-Regular', Menlo, monospace;
    }
    .embed-code code {
      background: none;
      border: 0;
      padding: 0;
      color: inherit;
      white-space: pre;
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
